---
import FutureTechMissionFrame from '../../../../components/FutureTechMissionFrame.astro';
---
<FutureTechMissionFrame
  missionNumber="2"
  title="Make It Think"
  tagline="Make your micro:bit remember, choose, and decide."
  question="How can code remember information, create unpredictable results, and make a decision?"
  success="I can use a variable, create a random value, and use one IF condition to decide what happens."
>
  <section id="stage-1" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">01</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">RECONNECT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Set Up</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Get your numbered kit and reopen your coding brain with a very quick Mission 1 reboot.</p>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Computer</span><span>☐ micro:bit</span><span>☐ USB data cable</span><span>☐ Mission page open</span></div>
    <div class="step-card"><strong>Mission 1 Reboot</strong><p>Open your saved Mission 1 project <b>if it is easy to find</b>. Change what Button A displays, then test it in the simulator. If you cannot find it within 2 minutes, skip the reboot and continue.</p></div>
    <div class="partner-strip"><span><strong>DRIVER</strong><small>Controls the computer and micro:bit.</small></span><span><strong>NAVIGATOR</strong><small>Reads the next step, predicts results, and checks requirements.</small></span></div>
    <p class="success">At Stage 3, switch roles. Both partners must be able to explain the code.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-2" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">02</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">REMEMBER</p><h2 class="stage-title">First Code — Variables</h2></div></div>
    <p class="concept">A <b>variable</b> is information your program remembers. Think of it as a labelled memory box.</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>1 — Open MakeCode</strong><p>Choose <b>New Project</b>. Name it <code>FirstName_L1_M2</code>.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>2 — Create score</strong><p>Create a variable named <code>score</code>. In <code>on start</code>, use <code>set score to 0</code>.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>3 — Count up</strong><p>Button A: <code>change score by 1</code>, then <code>show number score</code>.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>4 — Count down</strong><p>Button B: <code>change score by -1</code>, then show the score.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="success">✓ You should see: A makes the remembered score go up. B makes it go down.</p>
    <p class="warning">Common bug: if the score always stays at 1, check whether you used <b>SET</b> instead of <b>CHANGE</b>.</p>
    <div class="concept"><b>SET replaces. CHANGE adjusts.</b><br />If score = 4: SET score to 1 → 1. CHANGE score by 1 → 5.</div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-3" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">03</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">REMEMBER → DECIDE → OUTPUT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Make It React</h2></div></div>
    <p class="success"><b>SWITCH ROLES NOW.</b></p>
    <div class="route"><span>INPUT: Shake</span><span>REMEMBER: Random number</span><span>DECIDE: IF question</span><span>OUTPUT: Result</span></div>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge A — Random Choice</strong><p>Create a variable named <code>number</code>. On shake, set it to <code>pick random 1 to 6</code>, then show the number.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge B — Decision: IF</strong><p>After showing the number, add <code>IF number = 6</code>, then show a special icon.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>What does RANDOM mean?</strong><p>Unpredictable does <b>not</b> mean always different. The same number can appear twice.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>What does IF mean?</strong><p>IF asks a yes/no question. <b>TRUE</b> → run the blocks inside. <b>FALSE</b> → skip them.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="concept">Predict before testing: What happens if <code>number = 4</code>? What happens if <code>number = 6</code>?</p>
    <p class="success">Shake several times. If 6 does not appear, explain when the special response <i>would</i> happen and keep moving.</p>
    <p class="warning">Order matters: choose the random number first, then check the IF condition.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-4" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">04</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">YOUR CREATION</p><h2 class="stage-title">Build It — Chance Machine</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Create a Chance Machine that chooses a random result and gives a special response when one chosen condition is true.</p>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ A named variable stores the random value</span><span>☐ The program uses an input event</span><span>☐ It has a visible output</span><span>☐ It uses one IF condition</span><span>☐ The value is chosen before the condition is checked</span><span>☐ It runs on the real micro:bit</span><span>☐ You changed the range, result, icon, message, or theme</span></div>
    <p class="mini-label">Choose a theme or invent your own</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Lucky Number</strong><p>Shake 1–6. One number triggers a celebration.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Treasure Hunt</strong><p>Shake 1–5. One value discovers the treasure.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Critical Hit</strong><p>Shake 1–10. The highest value triggers a special attack.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Mystery Machine</strong><p>Create a different random theme with one special outcome.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="try4"><strong>STUCK? TRY 4</strong><p>1. CHECK your blocks. 2. SIMULATE the newest code. 3. DOWNLOAD the newest version. 4. PARTNER — explain what should happen. Still stuck? Ask for help and say what you already tried.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-5" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">05</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">OPTIONAL CHALLENGE</p><h2 class="stage-title">Level It Up</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Only after the Chance Machine works. Choose one while you wait for your checkpoint.</p>
    <div class="level-grid">
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Try Again</strong><p>Add ELSE so the program gives a different response when the IF is false.</p></article>
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Change the Odds</strong><p>Change the random range. Decide whether the special result is more or less likely.</p></article>
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Two Special Results</strong><p>Add another IF condition for a second special value.</p></article>
      <article class="level-card"><strong>Keep Score</strong><p>Add a <code>wins</code> variable and increase it when the special result happens.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="success">When every Build It box is checked, add your name or pair to the Ready-for-Check queue. Keep Leveling Up until you are called.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-6" class="stage checkpoint">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">06</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SHOW WHAT YOU KNOW</p><h2 class="stage-title">Checkpoint</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Bring your micro:bit and open your code when you are called. Each student completes the checkpoint individually.</p>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Check 1 — Remember It</strong><p>Point to one variable. Explain what information it remembers and give one value it could hold.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Check 2 — Explain the Decision</strong><p>Point to your IF condition. Explain the yes/no question it asks and when the blocks inside will run.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>Check 3 — Change It</strong><p>Change the winning value, random range, or special output. Then test it.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><strong>After Your Check</strong><p><b>PASS</b> = Mission Complete. <b>NOT YET</b> = fix one skill and retry.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage passport">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">✓</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SKILL PASSPORT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Mission 2 Skills</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I can create and use a variable</span><span>☐ I can change a variable's value</span><span>☐ I can generate a random value</span><span>☐ I can use one IF condition</span><span>☐ I can change, test, and explain my code</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage reset">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">↺</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">LEAVE IT READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Reset</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Project saved correctly</span><span>☐ micro:bit back in the numbered kit</span><span>☐ USB cable loosely coiled</span><span>☐ Kit complete and workspace clear</span><span>☐ Damage or missing equipment reported</span></div>
    <p class="concept">Exit question: What is one thing your program remembered or decided today?</p>
  </section>
</FutureTechMissionFrame>
